# Cursor agent rules — a-roofers-open-brain

These rules mirror `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` so Cursor agents behave identically to every other harness. **`CONVENTIONS.md` is the shared contract — read it first.** When anything here disagrees with `CONVENTIONS.md`, the contract wins.

## Read first (every task)
- `CONVENTIONS.md` — the contract (atoms, trust tiers, security/consent boundaries, design system, §13 wrap-up).
- `CLAUDE.md` — hard rules + Live⇄Dev alignment + memory budget.
- `AGENTS.md` — workforce + parallel-agent worktree discipline.
- Startup memory: `context/SOUL.md`, `context/USER.md`, `context/MEMORY.md`, today's `context/memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`. (No SessionStart hook fires in Cursor — read these manually.)

## Hard rules (the line stops if you break these)
- No destructive SQL or git. Migrations additive/idempotent; archive, never delete atoms.
- No secrets, service-role keys, or raw PII in committed files or curated memory.
- Trust-tier discipline: inferred memory is `evidence`; only humans/Quality Control promote to `instruction`.
- Security boundary: Historian internal-only, Researcher external-only. Consent-gated cross-client sharing only.
- Property-first and era-aware: place atoms carry `property_id`; code/material/practice atoms carry `era_of_practice`.
- Clean, professional language everywhere.
- Live⇄Dev: branch from the deployed/live branch (do not assume `main`), commit early, converge back — never fork lineages.
- Third-party agent tool gate: no external skill/plugin/MCP/agent wrapper/memory tool/installer becomes global or gets copied into the brain without A3 traceability, license/provenance review, egress review, installer/permission review, SkillSpector static scan where applicable, local-MCP compliance, rollback path, and human approval. Current decisions: `docs/54-third-party-agent-tool-gate-2026-06-25.md`.
- QuickBooks Online production is read-only / mirror-only: never create/update/delete/void/pay in live QBO; extract to Supabase/Open Brain only (`QUICKBOOKS_ACCESS_MODE=read_only`, `QUICKBOOKS_WRITE_ENABLED=false`, `docs/74-quickbooks-production-read-only-guardrails.md`, PEC-98).

## Session wrap-up / handoff — canonical: `CONVENTIONS.md` §13
Trigger: user says *"handoff"*, *"wrapup"*, *"wrap up"*, *"end of session"*, *"tie off"* — or context ~50%. Run in order, don't stop until the tree is clean and converged:

1. Finish the block, then commit completed work.
2. Clean the tree — `git status --short` must end **empty**: gitignore scratch/logs/byproducts, `git rm --cached` tracked-but-ignorable files, delete junk, commit real content. Never commit secrets/PII.
3. Update memory — today's daily-log block; `MEMORY.md`/`USER.md` only if something durable changed.
4. Converge — `git fetch origin`, confirm the live branch, merge the `contrib/*` branch in and **push**.
5. Agent alignment — if any rule or this procedure changed, propagate it to **all** harness files (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CONVENTIONS.md` §13, `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, plus any new ones) and commit. Never let the harness files contradict each other or CONVENTIONS §13.
6. Report and stop — branch, last commit, `tree clean ✓`, next task, blockers. Do not start the next task.

## Working rules (operational)
- **Structured source before OCR.** Before building any OCR/parse/extraction step, check whether the vendor API/`raw` JSON already carries the field — verify against the live DB first. Don't OCR what's already structured.
- **The agent deploys; the gate is explain-then-ship.** Full GitHub/Coolify/Hetzner access (corrected 2026-06-29, supersedes the prior human-only rule). Converge → `main`, apply migrations, build + tests green; then state change + impact + rollback, push `origin main`, and poll `/healthz` `buildCommit` to live. Self-granting via `settings.json` stays blocked and isn't needed.
- **Long-list disclosure (app-wide UI).** Any surface that can render an unbounded list opens showing **10 rows**, with the rest behind a `Show all N …` control; revealing them keeps the pane **exactly 10 rows tall** so it scrolls internally and the page doesn't grow. Same height collapsed and expanded, so the wheel only changes owner as the result of a click. Measure the height, never hardcode; persist reveal state in `localStorage`; filter before paging. Contract + the sticky-header traps a bounded pane forces: `standards/design/v1.md` § Long-list disclosure, `CONVENTIONS.md` §11a.
- **UOM & pricing (any price comparison).** Compare in **one** unit — ABC's pricing UOM (`priceQty.uom`, e.g. SQ), the unit agreements are quoted in. Canonical effective price is `abc_invoice_lines.price_per_uom` (`extendedPriceAmount ÷ priceQty.value`); align orders via `v_item_uom_map` (`unit_price × units_per_price_uom`). **Never** compare on `quantity`/`uom`/`unit_price`/`effective_unit_price`/`raw.pricePerUnitAmount` — per-stocking-unit or inconsistently ingested. Never fabricate a variance across mismatched units: flag `uom_mismatch`, leave variance NULL. New pricing surfaces read `price_per_uom` / `v_item_uom_map`. Migrations 119-122. Contract: `docs/46-uom-pricing-normalization.md`, `CONVENTIONS.md` §10c.
- **Price-agreement silos (any pricing join).** A negotiated price reaches an invoice line only through four gates: **vendor** (never join a branch by bare branch number — they collide across vendors, mig 208), **office** (resolved from the *invoice's* branch via `pricing_territory_office_id`; never shared between PE offices, mig 217), **time** (`effective_date <= invoice_date` plus **item-aware** version supersession — a newer version supersedes an older one only for the items it actually prices, so an item a shorter new list omits keeps its last known price; all agreements remain in effect until the vendor provides a new one, mig 277), and **UOM** (refuse, never convert). Fuzzy matching (trigram/colour-key) is always a fallback behind exact item number and exact description. The tie-break picks the **lowest** price, so simulate and diff before adding or backdating a book into an office that already has one. Credit memos never enter the price audit; returns invert the variance sign (filter `extended_price > 0`). A price list stays in effect until a **new list supersedes it** — `expiry_date` is documentary, recorded per agreement in `renewal_mode` (`evergreen` default | `expires`, mig 270). Read the audit through **`mv_invoice_audit_line`**, never `v_invoice_audit_line`: the view costs ~8.8s, over the 8s `statement_timeout`, so every PostgREST read of it fails and the surfaces render empty (migs 272–273). Contract: `docs/105-price-agreement-silo-rules.md`, `CONVENTIONS.md` §10b.
- **Vendor parity of the audit.** One eval per vendor; they differ **only** where the vendor's process differs. Legitimate differences (docs/81 d13 + open item 1): QXO has no agreements ever ⇒ every line valid as billed; SRS prices off the Level 4 sheet mapped to Richardson TX; PDF/OCR line-sum verification is ABC-only because no PDF source exists for SRS/QXO. Everything else — the four gates, UOM refusal, lowest-price tie-break, fuzzy fallback order, the No-Price `purchases_ytd >= 2` threshold, the credit-memo claim bar — is vendor-agnostic. Never special-case a vendor to make a number look right. Two open defects, do not copy: version supersession is ABC-only (SRS's lateral has no `effective_date` term, so a cheaper *older* sheet would win), and evergreen has two opposite NULL defaults across the arms (latent only — both tables default `'evergreen'`). Full table: [`CONVENTIONS.md`](CONVENTIONS.md) §10b.
- **Slack agents** — per-agent bot identities/app IDs/token env vars/channel IDs are in the `slack-agents` skill (`.claude/skills/slack-agents/`). A Slack config token can't mint/read bot tokens.
